# Intervals.icu API Configuration
#
# API_KEY and ATHLETE_ID are the ONLY source of credentials. Tools do not accept
# them as arguments; every request uses the values set here.

# Base URL (Optional, defaults to https://intervals.icu/api/v1)
# INTERVALS_API_BASE_URL=https://intervals.icu/api/v1

# Required: Your Intervals.icu API Key
API_KEY=your_intervals_api_key_here

# Required: Your Intervals.icu Athlete ID
ATHLETE_ID=your_athlete_id_here

# HTTP Transport + OAuth 2.0 — SELF-HOSTING ONLY (do not set on Prefect Horizon)
#
# Leave everything below unset for local stdio use (no auth needed) and on
# Prefect Horizon: Horizon fronts the server with its own OAuth gateway, and
# setting the MCP_* vars there stacks a second provider on top, causing 403s.
# On Horizon set only API_KEY and ATHLETE_ID.
#
# Self-hosting (e.g. a container) — serve over HTTP:
# MCP_TRANSPORT=http
# FASTMCP_HOST=0.0.0.0
# Port your platform routes to (defaults to 8000):
# FASTMCP_PORT=8000
#
# Then set all three vars below to protect the endpoint with the built-in
# single-client OAuth provider (authorization code + PKCE, no dynamic client
# registration; the client secret is issued as the bearer token). Run exactly
# one instance.
#
# Steps:
#   1. Choose any string for MCP_CLIENT_ID (e.g. "intervals-mcp")
#   2. Generate a long random MCP_CLIENT_SECRET:
#        python -c "import secrets;print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
#   3. Set MCP_SERVER_URL to the public HTTPS URL of this server (no /mcp)
#   4. In Claude → Customize (or Settings) → Connectors → Add custom connector:
#        Name                = intervals
#        URL                 = <MCP_SERVER_URL>/mcp
#        Advanced settings → Use your own OAuth client:
#          OAuth Client ID     = <MCP_CLIENT_ID>
#          OAuth Client Secret = <MCP_CLIENT_SECRET>
#
# MCP_CLIENT_ID=intervals-mcp
# MCP_CLIENT_SECRET=your_long_random_secret_here
# MCP_SERVER_URL=https://your-host.example.com
